e\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 7 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+6{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 25 & -25\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-4 \\\\ 25{x}_{3}=-25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-1.$ Substituting this into the second   equation yields\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+3(-1)=-4\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-1.\n$$\n\n Finally,  by substituting ${x}_{2}=-1$ and ${x}_{3}=-1$ into the first equation we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+(-1)-(-1)=1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=1+(-1)+(-1)=-1.\n$$" :questio