rom third equation we get ${x}_{3}=-1$ and substituting this value into the second equation yields ${x}_{2}=-2(-1)+3=5.$ Finally, substituting ${x}_{2}=5$ and ${x}_{3}=-1$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+2(5)+2(-1)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=(-6)+5+(-1)=-2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-112254/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ed6a6ea8-6100-5224-b75f-b87c037fafbb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-112254"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-112290/selection/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" :answer/id #uuid "e4358d53-13b0-503e-9697-3b1c613288be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112290/selection/f6dab1aaf947cb8c1f47690c13a34f270ff23312486a212e76af727dcf7e93a5" :answer/id #uuid "4e038d1b-3331-5f0f-aaab-4958a4fcf275" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112290/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "45f36f6c-2a0d-5fd1-885d-5825febe7a9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112290/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer/id #uuid "04592154-8275-54f6-ac3e-d46ae5ba5c29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112290/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "da716534-f13e-55e9-a30e-2d7d4db20d52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112290/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "69c9437d-d6f2-522b-acd1-be87eacf7327" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-112290/selection/f6dab1aaf947cb8c1f47690c13a34f270ff23312486a212e76af727dcf7e93a5" :answer-field/choices ["q-112290/selection/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" "q-112290/selection/f6dab1aaf947cb8c1f47690c13a34f270ff23312486a212e76af727dcf7e93a5" "q-112290/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-112290/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" "q-112290/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-112290" :question/id #uuid "a8846d68-6963-5870-b9c9-f845b4e15577" :question/math-academy-id "q-112290" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -8 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 5 & 11 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -8 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 5 & 11 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -8 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 5 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 & -14 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -8 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -5 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 & -14 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 15\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(-\\frac{3}{7}){R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -5 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 & -14 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 21\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ -{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}=11 \\\\ 13{x}_{3}=-14 \\\\ 0=21,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere the fourth equation is always false. Therefore, the system has no solution and we conclude that \n\n$$\nx\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-112290/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ed6a6ea8-6100-5224-b75f-b87c037fafbb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-112290"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-35215/selection/cedce138738816f1e959edfd5049bf0c6bcf0acc69b898c7f84479cb3a782ce3" :answer/id #uuid "29e36e20-5abc-55d2-8940-fb7f906a56d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35215/selection/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818" :answer/id #uuid "886135d8-6646-5f8a-a0d6-517284e12a49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35215/selection/81ec9cf26b4d634e9c6dd41dfa456114165178124fc4fbd86ade95b2369b8a6b" :answer/id #uuid "ba9aa707-2b1b-514d-9bd0-77e54292c3d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35215/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "ee366eb7-ff92-544e-acff-f2fe294f8874" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35215/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "14496d3e-c699-5465-8a7c-516de81b4ab5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35215/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1aaad9f9-75cd-58bf-91cb-79696edfb796" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-35215/selection/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818" :answer-field/choices ["q-35215/selection/cedce138738816f1e959edfd5049bf0c6bcf0acc69b898c7f84479cb3a782ce3" "q-35215/selection/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818" "q-35215/selection/81ec9cf26b4d634e9c6dd41dfa456114165178124fc4fbd86ade95b2369b8a6b" "q-35215/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-35215/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-35215" :question/id #uuid "5588391a-4fdc-5cf6-95da-5270d6aba8aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-35215" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 16 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 16 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 0 & 10 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 6 & 10 & -2 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 10 & 0 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 0 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 10 & -2 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 10 & 0 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 0 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 10 & 0 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 0 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=10 \\\\ 5{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ -2{x}_{3}=-4 \\\\ 0=0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the fourth equation, we get a true statement. Then, from the second and third equation, we get ${x}_{2}=1$ and  ${x}_{3}=2$ respectively. Substituting ${x}_{2}=1$ into the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n3{x}_{1}+5(1)=10\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=\\frac{5}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}=\\frac{5}{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-35215/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ed6a6ea8-6100-5224-b75f-b87c037fafbb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-35215"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-112291/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "13feff4e-4c01-5c8d-8721-82eb17217dc8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112291/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "0d432010-0996-558f-a9c2-e1a86a89f7fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112291/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "11f75782-b43d-5372-b336-d602cbdcda0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112291/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "72e536f4-dcd7-5d2e-aa5f-e4711843b0ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112291/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "d1ee3478-6d48-5a19-a168-5f5be0113705" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112291/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6a626df3-8254-5e86-9389-2a4ca861e81d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-112291/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-112291/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-112291/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-112291/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-112291/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-112291/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-112291" :question/id #uuid "c2042116-edb5-5539-a4f7-320326e77b07" :question/math-academy-id "q-112291" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -15 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -15 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 7 \\\\ -2 & -3 & -2 & -15 \\\\ 4 & -2 & -4 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -2 & -4 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -4 & -22\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-6){R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & -16\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=7 \\\\ -{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=-1 \\\\ 8{x}_{3}=-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom third equation we get ${x}_{3}=-2$ and substituting this value into the second equation yields ${x}_{2}=-2(-2)+1=5.$ Finally, substituting ${x}_{2}=5$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+5=7\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=2+5+(-2)=5.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-112291/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ed6a6ea8-6100-5224-b75f-b87c037fafbb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-112291"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4823"] :question/problem "Find the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ if $\\,\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\},$ and\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/assets/0ef553621590325eecc2b429ffa09cd0cd4645a2653b3fd93db25f711676c132.png)" :question/worked-solution "We know that any vector in  $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\}$ has the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $x_1$ and $x_2$ are the coordinates relative to the basis $\\,\\mathcal{B}.$ Since we are told that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/assets/93ae6d0ad6dbd6036c99e5d2fcb55789fef9b2e576300f13b43ed561856fa218.png) we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={{(-1)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{{(\\,3\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6282"] :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\},$ where\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/assets/dc9eaa6ef7632676a920b5032f9af213dba581552c2337471b4657a0fc26ad2f.png)" :question/worked-solution "Remember, the order of the vectors in a basis is important.\n\nNotice that \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/assets/9ed5651afa52eedb2786ed4e46875636e9263f955f9c99db563ff3ebe629275f.png)\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x} = (-5) \\cdot \\mathbf{b}_1 + 2 \\cdot \\mathbf{b}_2\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/assets/5972542de3b4c7c622177994f83239fb14f4ea3242cdc164a88b102b780b7da9.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4824"] :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\},$ where\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/assets/d094c88349d0a2c8707fafcf1a1cd63de028d56358ba8019b0527e77091e51d5.png)" :question/worked-solution "We need to find $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/assets/14c42b3d306468a8a17f5ffaef535dd39c6d5fdb079366d9f495774b6e019815.png)\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 5 & -11 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -12 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix above corresponds to the following system of equations: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ -4{x}_{2}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $x_2 =-1.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\nx_1 + 3 \\left( -1 \\right)  = -5\n\\qquad \\Longrightarrow \\qquad\nx_1 = -2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/assets/5e92e3cfdbf8d1c81be5b47124df9992d98835668154a50ece28cce8941860ca.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4825"] :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2, \\mathbf{b}_3 \\},$ where\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/assets/4eb4b3533453f1a2c08c98bb8e6fd63e3f93563a4a2d56ecc0c0caef225b82e3.png)" :question/worked-solution "We need to find $x_1,$ $x_2,$ and $x_3$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above system as an augmented matrix $M$ and reducing using Gaussian elimination, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{3}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{4}{3} & \\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ -9{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=7 \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}{x}_{3}=\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $x_3 =2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n-9x_2 - 2 = 7 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad x_2 = -1,\n$$\n\nand substituting $x_2=-1$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_1+3(-1) = 1 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_1 = 4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/assets/61d8401f40152a8eaeb30d3dc55d9548cac508b6239a9a70e99fbed9e271805b.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
